### Option (a): Identify Whether an Inputted Year is a Leap Year or Not

**C Program:**
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int year;
    printf("Enter a year: ");
    scanf("%d", &year);
    if ((year % 400 == 0) || (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0))
    {
        printf("%d is a leap year.\n", year);
    }
    else
    {
        printf("%d is not a leap year.\n", year);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

**2025 Syllabus JavaScript Equivalent:**
```javascript
let year = Number(prompt("Enter a year:"));
if ((year % 400 === 0) || (year % 4 === 0 && year % 100 !== 0)) {
    document.write(year + " is a leap year.");
} else {
    document.write(year + " is not a leap year.");
}
```

### Option (b): Print the First Ten Numbers of the Fibonacci Series Using `for` Loop

**C Program:**
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int i, n = 10, t1 = 0, t2 = 1, nextTerm;
    printf("First 10 numbers of Fibonacci series: ");
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++)
    {
        printf("%d ", t1);
        nextTerm = t1 + t2;
        t1 = t2;
        t2 = nextTerm;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

**2025 Syllabus JavaScript Equivalent:**
```javascript
let t1 = 0, t2 = 1, nextTerm;
for (let i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    document.write(t1 + " ");
    nextTerm = t1 + t2;
    t1 = t2;
    t2 = nextTerm;
}
```
